<p>Note: (a)  Effective January 1, 1995, the company adopted Statement of Financial Accounting Standards No. 116, &quot;Accounting for Contributions Received and Contributions Made,&quot; resulting in a charge of $7.8 million.</p>
<p>The cumulative effect reflects the after tax charge to establish a liability for the present value of the company's total outstanding charitable commitments as of January 1, 1995.</p>
<p>Certain amounts for the 1995 periods have been reclassified to conform to 1996 classifications.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
